  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are largely safe on incident reporting and recall triggers, but S2 is weakened by allowing sales to continue above the 5% limit up to an 8% cap during an unbounded regulator-set corrective period, with no fixed transition deadline. S3 and S4 land in acceptable ranges with a 72-month retrofit deadline and 36-month suppression deadline, while S5 sets a mandatory 8/100k recall trigger but omits a serious-injury recall clause. The deal respects the red lines on public disclosure and customer access to per-model results."
